cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Engram Memory: a project memory that stays aligned with your code"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and keep the attribution (MIT)."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: max423
repository-code: "https://github.com/max423/engram-memory"
url: "https://github.com/max423/engram-memory"
abstract: >-
  engram is a curated, git-native, token-minimal project memory for coding
  assistants: a markdown knowledge base of decisions plus a code-aligned context
  map that updates itself as you work. The deterministic core (index, BM25 search,
  graph, change-detection) runs with zero tokens; the LLM is used only for synthesis.
keywords:
  - project-memory
  - llm
  - claude-code
  - git-native
  - token-minimal
  - bm25
license: MIT
